# Local secrets file (compose env_file + dev overrides; see .env.example).
# Never tracked: it holds API keys and endpoint URLs. (WP-9: the portable
# deployment guide instructs creating this file, so it must not be committable.)
.env
# Local docs/ content is never tracked: fresh clones have no docs/ until WP-2
# lands env-driven resolution, and any local copy stays untracked — this rule
# only stops git from re-tracking it.
# --- Past task/session run history: NEVER commit (leak guard) ---
# Task runs accumulate prompts, full transcripts, stage reports and
# tool output that cannot be guaranteed free of sensitive information.
# Curated docs are tracked in-repo (docs-symlink reversal, 2026-10-26);
# run history is not, including engine task storage that now lands in
# in-repo docs/tasks/ for the kainbain project itself.
# Current store (2,069 session files, ~679 MB at Oct 2026):
.kainbain/sessions/
# Task storage is TRACKED (2026-10-27 decision): Runner worktrees commit
# docs/tasks/<id>/ files (plans, reports) and push them so the backend can
# see them; the old history was moved to ~/archive/kainbain-tasks-* first.
# Session transcripts stay ignored below.
# Any future per-task/session artefact dropped at repo root or in scratch:
scratch/sessions/
*.session.jsonl
# Session transcripts dropped at repo root (e.g. 2026-...Z_<id>.jsonl): never commit (leak guard).
/*.jsonl

# Live task snapshots are engine store state, never branch content (Step 5,
# 2026-11-11): the backend rewrites docs/tasks/<id>/task.md on every save.
# Keeping them ignored means `git add -A` can never re-track them and —
# decisive for the branch-switch bug that stranded tasks 82e49a05 and
# 9d2b75a2 — git's own checkout safety never refuses a switch because of
# them (ignored untracked files do not block `git checkout`). Plans and
# reports under docs/tasks/<id>/ stay tracked. Custom docs dir names are
# covered dynamically by the backend's clean-tree guard, not by this file.
docs/tasks/*/task.md
